https://s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/freemius/plugins/3564/banner.png\";s:15:\"card_banner_url\";s:72:\"https://s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/freemius/plugins/3564/card_banner.png\";s:15:\"selling_point_0\";N;s:15:\"selling_point_1\";N;s:15:\"selling_point_2\";N;s:11:\"screenshots\";N;s:2:\"id\";s:3:\"751\";s:7:\"updated\";s:19:\"2020-06-17 18:28:20\";s:7:\"created\";s:19:\"2019-04-01 16:45:54\";s:22:\"\0FS_Entity\0_is_updated\";b:0;}s:10:\"is_premium\";b:0;s:14:\"premium_suffix\";s:9:\"(Premium)\";s:7:\"is_live\";b:1;s:9:\"bundle_id\";N;s:17:\"bundle_public_key\";N;s:17:\"opt_in_moderation\";N;s:10:\"public_key\";s:32:\"pk_7e0e413b0ffb7551b21cf57501455\";s:10:\"secret_key\";N;s:2:\"id\";s:4:\"3564\";s:7:\"updated\";s:19:\"2026-03-16 12:35:38\";s:7:\"created\";s:19:\"2019-04-01 16:27:41\";s:22:\"\0FS_Entity\0_is_updated\";b:0;}i:1;O:9:\"FS_Plugin\":24:{s:16:\"parent_plugin_id\";s:4:\"3072\";s:5:\"title\";s:13:\"Gravity Forms\";s:4:\"slug\";s:31:\"wp-fail2ban-addon-gravity-forms\";s:12:\"premium_slug\";s:39:\"wp-fail2ban-addon-gravity-forms-premium\";s:4:\"type\";s:6:\"plugin\";s:20:\"affiliate_moderation\";N;s:19:\"is_wp_org_compliant\";b:1;s:22:\"premium_releases_count\";i:0;s:4:\"file\";N;s:7:\"version\";N;s:11:\"auto_update\";N;s:4:\"info\";O:14:\"FS_Plugin_Info\":13:{s:9:\"plugin_id\";s:4:\"3565\";s:11:\"description\";s:180:\"<p>No matter how good your anti-spam measures, some will get past. This add-on logs spam form submissions via <b>WP fail2ban</b>, and provides a new filter for <i>fail2ban</i>.</p>\";s:17:\"short_description\";s:58:\"Integration with Gravity Forms: log spam form submissions.\";s:10:\"banner_url\";s:67:\"https://s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/freemius/plugins/3565/banner.png\";s:15:\"card_banner_url\";s:72:\"https://s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/freemius/plugins/3565/card_banner.png\";s:15:\"selling_point_0\";s:0:\"\";s:15:\"selling_point_1\";N;s:15:\"selling_point_2\";N;s:11:\"screenshots\";N;s:2:\"id\";s:3:\"752\";s:7:\"updated\";s:19:\"2019-04-10 07:48:36\";s:7:\"created\";s:19:\"2019-04-01 17:49:23\";s:22:\"\0FS_Entity\0_is_updated\";b:0;}s:10:\"is_premium\";b:0;s:14:\"premium_suffix\";s:9:\"(Premium)\";s:7:\"is_live\";b:1;s:9:\"bundle_id\";N;s:17:\"bundle_public_key\";N;s:17:\"opt_in_moderation\";N;s:10:\"public_key\";s:32:\"pk_8c5d4d69296f78a9827a02d66732b\";s:10:\"secret_key\";N;s:2:\"id\";s:4:\"3565\";s:7:\"updated\";s:19:\"2026-03-15 02:19:20\";s:7:\"created\";s:19:\"2019-04-01 17:45:47\";s:22:\"\0FS_Entity\0_is_updated\";b:0;}i:2;O:9:\"FS_Plugin\":24:{s:16:\"parent_plugin_id\";s:4:\"3072\";s:5:\"title\";s:21:\"WP fail2ban Blocklist\";s:4:\"slug\";s:21:\"wpf2b-addon-blocklist\";s:12:\"premium_slug\";s:27:\"wp-fail2ban-addon-blocklist\";s:4:\"type\";s:6:\"plugin\";s:20:\"affiliate_moderation\";N;s:19:\"is_wp_org_compliant\";b:1;s:22:\"premium_releases_count\";i:20;s:4:\"file\";N;s:7:\"version\";N;s:11:\"auto_update\";N;s:4:\"info\";O:14:\"FS_Plugin_Info\":13:{s:9:\"plugin_id\";s:4:\"6750\";s:11:\"description\";s:1071:\"<p>There are many plugins that use a database to check for malicious IPs <b>after</b> they connect, and of course <tt>fail2ban</tt> stops <i>repeated</i> attacks, but what if bad IPs could be blocked <b>before</b> they connect?</p>\n<p>By working collaboratively - sharing attack data - <i>WP fail2ban Blocklist</i> does exactly that.</p>\n<h3>How</h3>\n<p>The Blocklist Network Service (BNS) collects attack data from participating sites, performs some analytical magic, and sends back a list of IPs that are attacking sites now but haven\'t yet attacked that site.</p>\n<p>In other words, each site regularly gets a unique list of IPs to block <b>preemptively</b>.</p>\n<h3>GDPR</h3>\n<p>The BNS doesn\'t collect personal data, and bots don\'t have rights.</p>\n<p>That said, the BNS only collects the minimum data required (time, IP, event), and only for IPs that have behaved maliciously.</p>\n<p>Of course, it is possible that some data is generated by <i>people</i> behaving maliciously, but the BNS 